// Multi-voice augmentation-dot direction. LilyPond's \voiceOne/\voiceTwo set
// Dots.direction on the WHOLE voice (UP for odd voices, DOWN for even), so the
// down voice's dotted b (B4, the treble middle line) takes its dot in the space
// BELOW the line. A collision whose shift moves the UP group right overrides the
// down voice's dots back to UP; here the second b/c' is a touch, the DOWN group
// moves right (negative shift), and the voice-props direction stands.
// LILYPOND-REF: scm/music-functions.scm:616-631 direction-polyphonic-grobs — Dots
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/note-collision.cc:374-397 check_meshing_chords — set_property direction
// MEASURED (scratch/lpreg/dot-force-down-twin.ly, LilyPond 2.26.0): the dot prints
// half a space BELOW the middle line, and the b head +1.30 right of the c' head.
// An earlier header here declared "forced down off the staff line" a Lily#-own
// rule; the OUTCOME was right for this book, the mechanism was not. The part was
// also renamed p → m: p became a reserved word (dynamics) and the exporter
// refused the book with LYS0002 while the snapshot path kept rendering it.
octave absolute
time 2/4
part m { clef treble }
section Main {
  m {
    voice { c'4 c'4 }
    { b4. b8 }
  }
}
form main { Main }
score main "dot-force-down" { staff m }
